7. Known limitations and pending verification
- HRRP Start Date originally uses MM-DD-YYYY formatting, while End Date uses MM/DD/YYYY formatting.
- Date conversion in the earlier cleaning process resulted in NULL dates and needs correction if dates are required later.
- Suppressed HRRP records do not provide discharge denominators, so their readmission rates cannot be calculated.
- Some hospitals have no matching HRRP records, and these must remain distinguishable from N/A.
- The six-condition status validation query has not yet been completed; only AMI has been verified in the final analysis table.
- The total row count of hospital_readmission_analysis should still be checked independently.
- National and state weighted benchmarking calculations have been planned conceptually but have not yet been implemented or validated.

Current status: The cleaned source tables and combined hospital-level analysis table have been created, and the one-row-per-hospital duplicate check and AMI status check have passed. The remaining validation is to check all six conditions and confirm the final table row count.
